## Working process

- Review EDK2-generated `edk2.cdx.json` first when evaluating compliance.
- Update `docs/uefi/conformance.md` after any attribute implementation change.
- File new drafting issues in `docs/uefi/known_doc_issues.md` as they are found.
- Do not commit `docs/uefi/` files — they stay gitignored (local-only working copies). The directory is `.gitignored` precisely so the private USBT draft (`UEFI SBOM Guidelines.docx`) and its derivatives never enter the public remote.

### Push / publish policy (documentation vs. implementation)

Any **"do not push"** caveat in USBT or working-group context applies to **guideline documentation only** (the Word draft, markdown mirrors, and conformance notes under `docs/uefi/`). Those materials stay local and off the public remote by design.

**Implementation** — code and tests that *implement* the guidelines (`uswid/`, `tests/`, `docs/source/` Sphinx docs that are not the private USBT draft, packaging, CI, etc.) follows normal open-source practice: commit and push when ready. There is no separate restriction on pushing compliance-related **code**; only the private guideline **documents** are scoped out of the remote.

